Project 3: Campus Placement Portal Backend

What it is. A backend for managing college placements. There are three types of users: students,
recruiters (company HR) and the placement officer (admin). Recruiters post jobs with eligibility criteria,
students apply if eligible, and the admin tracks everything.

Why it impresses. This is your flagship backend project. It shows real database design with many
related tables, role based access control, business rules, file uploads, testing and Docker. It is also a
domain you understand personally, so you can explain it confidently and with genuine examples.

Tech stack

Part                      Use       

Framework                 FastAPI
Database                  PostgreSQL with SQLAlchemy and Alembic
Auth                      JWT with roles: student, recruiter, admin
File storage              Resume upload, saved locally first, cloud storage later
Testing                   pytest, aiming for good coverage of business rules
Infra                     Docker and Docker Compose for the app and database
Automation                GitHub Actions to run tests on every push

Must have features
• Registration and login for all three roles with role based permissions.
• Student profile with CGPA, branch, skills and resume upload.
• Recruiters create job drives with minimum CGPA, eligible branches and last date.
• Students can only apply to drives they are eligible for, and only before the last date.
• Application status flow: applied, shortlisted, interview, selected, rejected.
• Admin dashboard endpoints: number of students placed, company wise offers, highest and average
package.
Extra features once the basics work
• Email notification when an application status changes, using background tasks.
• Search and filter jobs by company, role and package.
• Rate limiting on login to prevent misuse.
• A small React or Streamlit frontend for the student side.

